# systemUpdate — settings
#
# This file IS tracked in git, on purpose: every setting below is commented
# out, so a fresh clone runs correctly as-is and a reviewer can see exactly
# which values ship and which ones were changed. There is no separate template
# file, because there is no per-user value that needs hiding.
#
# Precedence, strongest first:
#   1. environment variables    SYSUPDATE_LOG_DIR="/tmp/opencode/fromconfig2"
#   2. this file
#   3. the built-in defaults noted under each setting
#
# This file is bash and is sourced by `lib/config.sh`. A `#` starts a comment;
# delete it and write your value to activate a setting. Every line here is bash
# syntax, so a typo is a real error, not silently ignored text.
#
# Changing a value here affects every future run of every machine that has this
# file. For a change that is yours alone, prefer the environment variable.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOG_DIR — where log files are written
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every run writes its full stdout + stderr to one file here.
# File name: systemUpdateYYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM.txt, and two runs in the same minute
# get -1, -2, ... so nothing is ever overwritten.
#
# LEAVE EMPTY to use the automatic cascade (preferred):
#   1. xdg-user-dir DOCUMENTS       -> localized "Documents" (e.g. Belgeler)
#   2. ~/.config/user-dirs.dirs     -> XDG_DOCUMENTS_DIR
#   3. English names                -> $HOME/Documents, $HOME/Document
#   4. Home backup (not hidden)     -> $HOME/systemUpdate
#   5. XDG state dir (last resort)  -> ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/systemUpdate
#
# To pin a specific directory, uncomment and set it:
# LOG_DIR="/tmp/opencode/fromconfig2"
LOG_DIR="/tmp/opencode/fromconfig2"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOG_KEEP — how many log files to keep
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# After each run the older ones are deleted automatically, keeping this many
# newest. This is the only place in the whole tool that deletes anything, and
# it only ever removes log files this tool wrote — never a package, a config
# file or a .pacnew.
#
# A value that is not a positive number is ignored and treated as "keep
# everything", so a typo here can never delete your logs.
#
# Default: 50
#LOG_KEEP=50


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SKIP_CHANNELS — channels that are never even asked about
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Space-separated channel ids, skipped without prompting.
# Valid ids come from the channel table in lib/apps.sh:
#
#   updated by the tool:  npm code pipx uv opencode claude codex pnpm pip go
#   reported only:        cargo docker flatpak dotnet composer gh
#
# Useful for a channel you never want touched, or one that is slow or noisy.
#
# Default: (none — every channel asks)
#SKIP_CHANNELS=""


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GO_BIN_DIR — where `go install` puts its binaries
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Go channel reads the module path embedded in each binary in this
# directory and reinstalls it with `go install <path>@latest`. Point it at
# your GOPATH bin folder.
#
# Default: $HOME/go/bin
#GO_BIN_DIR="$HOME/go/bin"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STATUS_AUR — include the AUR in --status
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# --status reports the official repositories only, because that check
# (checkupdates) is fast and offline. Setting this to 1 additionally runs
# `yay -Qua`, which fetches the AUR git repository: a network operation that
# can take seconds, so --status stops being a quick glance.
#
# Note that `yay -Qua` cannot report orphaned AUR packages either way — a
# package no longer in the AUR is invisible to every query.
#
# Default: 0 (off)
#STATUS_AUR=0